    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.icons\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen the current working directory has been deleted, opening a new file causes the following error if both `mini.icons` and `mini.tabline` are enabled:\n\n```\nE5108: Lua: vim/fs.lua:0: assertion failed!\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'assert'\n        vim/fs.lua: in function 'abspath'\n        vim/filetype.lua: in function 'filetype_match'\n        .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/icons.lua:2153: in function 'getter'\n        .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/icons.lua:475: in function 'get'\n        .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/icons.lua:2174: in function 'getter'\n        .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/icons.lua:475: in function 'get'\n        .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/tabline.lua:544: in function 'get_icon'\n        .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/tabline.lua:174: in function 'format'\n        .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/tabline.lua:390: in function 'finalize_labels'\n        .../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/tabline.lua:155: in function <.../.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/tabline.lua:150>\n```\n\nExpected behavior: Neovim opens the file without crashing.\n\nNeovim version: v0.12.2\nmini.nvim commit: ff8b3580935818ef2f21bdd651f057a2ae071eab\nOS: Debian\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Enable `mini.icons` and `mini.tabline` in `~/.config/nvim-repro/init.lua`:\n```lua\n-- assuming mini.nvim is available\nrequire('mini.icons').setup()\nrequire('mini.tabline').setup()\n```\n\n2. Create temporary directory, enter it and start Neovim:\n```bash\nmkdir /tmp/repro && cd /tmp/repro\nNVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim\n``` \n\n3. In a separate terminal, delete the directory:\n```bash\nrmdir /tmp/repro\n```\n\n4. Back in Neovim, try to edit a new file:\n```\n:e /tmp/file.txt\n```",
